.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-PASSWD 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-passwd
.Nd compute password hashes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl passwd
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl 1 ]
.Oo
.Fl apr1 ]
.Oo
.Fl aixmd5 ]
.Oo
.Fl 5 ]
.Oo
.Fl 6 ]
.Oo
.Fl salt
.Em string ]
.Oo
.Fl in
.Em file ]
.Oo
.Fl stdin ]
.Oo
.Fl noverify ]
.Oo
.Fl quiet ]
.Oo
.Fl table ]
.Oo
.Fl reverse ]
.Oo
.Fl rand
.Em files ]
.Oo
.Fl writerand
.Em file ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Oo
.Em password ]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command computes the hash of a password typed at run-time or the
hash of each password in a list.
The password list is taken from the named file for option
.Sy -in ,
from stdin for option
.Sy -stdin ,
or from the command line, or from the terminal otherwise.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -1
Use the MD5 based BSD password algorithm
.Sy 1
(default).
.It Sy -apr1
Use the
.Sy apr1
algorithm (Apache variant of the BSD algorithm).
.It Sy -aixmd5
Use the
.Sy AIX MD5
algorithm (AIX variant of the BSD algorithm).
.It Sy -5
.It Sy -6
Use the
.Sy SHA256
/
.Sy SHA512
based algorithms defined by Ulrich Drepper.
See
.Lk https://www.akkadia.org/drepper/SHA-crypt.txt .
.It Sy -salt Em string
Use the specified salt.
When reading a password from the terminal, this implies
.Sy -noverify .
.It Sy -in Em file
Read passwords from
.Em file .
.It Sy -stdin
Read passwords from
.Sy stdin .
.It Sy -noverify
Don't verify when reading a password from the terminal.
.It Sy -quiet
Don't output warnings when passwords given at the command line are
truncated.
.It Sy -table
In the output list, prepend the cleartext password and a TAB character
to each password hash.
.It Sy -reverse
When the
.Sy -table
option is used, reverse the order of cleartext and hash.
.It Sy -rand Em files Ns , Sy -writerand Em file
See
.Xr openssl 1
for details.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
  % openssl passwd -1 -salt xxxxxxxx password
  $1$xxxxxxxx$UYCIxa628.9qXjpQCjM4a.

  % openssl passwd -apr1 -salt xxxxxxxx password
  $apr1$xxxxxxxx$dxHfLAsjHkDRmG83UXe8K0

  % openssl passwd -aixmd5 -salt xxxxxxxx password
  xxxxxxxx$8Oaipk/GPKhC64w/YVeFD/
.Ed
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Sy -crypt
option was removed in OpenSSL 3.0.
